From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:56:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec_decode,sample): skip dead verification rows in
 sampler and sample DSpark top-k sparsely

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5 (tree ed1bdb7a7684da33d403a055521ac0c4dd7ca670).

Rationale:
1. When speculative block verification runs with a per-request verification cap (dead_row_cut from remaining max_tokens, adaptive confidence gating, or CED/local draft cuts) and non-temperature sampling parameters (top_k, top_p, min_p, penalties, logit_bias, bad_words, thinking_budget), RejectionSampler._verify previously passed the full [num_tokens, vocab_size] logits tensor to Sampler.apply_sampling_params without dead_row_cut. Every dead row past dead_row_cut[r] was copied from BF16 to FP32 (517 KB/row at V=129,280) and processed through bias, penalties, bad_words, thinking_budget, temperature, min_p, and tilelang_topk_topp before rejection_sample ignored all rows past dead_row_cut[r].
2. When DSparkSpeculator._sample_sequential_topk ran with dspark_draft_topk=K, it previously filled the entire [num_reqs, n_spec, vocab_size] base_logits buffer with -inf, scattered the K Markov-corrected candidate scores back into base_logits[:, i] at each step, and launched full-vocabulary argmax or 127-block gumbel_sample + gumbel_finish over all 129,280 columns per step.

Changes:
1. Add tilelang_inputs.mask_dead_rows to compute live_idx_mapping (-1 on dead rows where row - cu_num_logits[r] > dead_row_cut[r]) and per-row (row_top_k, row_top_p) (neutral vocab_size and 1.0 on dead rows) in a single 1-block launch when dead_row_cut is present and processed logprobs are not requested.
2. Thread live_idx_mapping into tilelang_sampling.copy_logits, logit_bias, penalties, bad_words, thinking_budget, temperature, and min_p so dead verification rows exit before reading or writing vocabulary rows, and pass (row_top_k, row_top_p) directly into tilelang_topk_topp.apply_top_k_top_p.
3. Add apply_markov_bias_topk on DSparkDeepseekV4ForCausalLM and Qwen3DSparkForCausalLM / DSparkMarkovHead, and add tilelang_sampling.topk_greedy_sample and tilelang_sampling.topk_gumbel_sample (keying Philox draws and tie-breaking by each candidate's global vocabulary index and maintaining draft_logits by clearing only the previous step's K candidate indices before writing the new K candidates).

Quality:
Bit-exact on all live verification rows, verified tokens, drafted tokens, and cached draft_logits across greedy and stochastic sampling; also prevents NaN or near-uniform unverified dead rows from perturbing or stalling Sampler.apply_sampling_params.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/worker/test_dead_rows.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dspark_topk.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dspark_v41_gathered_markov.py tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_sampling_states_gather.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_copy_logits.py tests/v1/worker/test_prepare_kernels.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_tilelang_rejection.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_rejection_sampler_utils.py (935 passed across 2 boots on GB10).

Upstream status: local speculative-decoding and TileLang sampler optimization for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on GB10.
